        <div class="teaser tui_teaser_hr tui_teaser_hr_img_left">





	<div class="cmp-teaser">
	
   <div class="cmp-teaser-container">
      <div class="cmp-teaser__content">
         
    

         
    <h2 class="cmp-teaser__title">
        Overview
    </h2>

         
    <div class="cmp-teaser__description"><p><i>Women, Business and the Law</i> assesses how laws and policies shape women’s economic participation at different stages of their working lives across 10 topics: Safety, Mobility, Work, Pay, Marriage, Parenthood, Childcare, Entrepreneurship, Assets, and Pension, reflecting the evolving legal environment faced by women as employees and entrepreneurs. Each topic is assessed using a three-pillar methodology that examines legal frameworks, supportive frameworks, and enforcement perceptions, capturing how laws operate in practice.</p>
</div>

         
    

      </div>
      
      
   </div>
</div>

    







</div>

        
    </div>



            </div>
                
         
     </div>
                


            
</div>
